{"study_accession":"PRJNA872401","secondary_study_accession":"SRP394229","title":"Circulating monocytes associated with anti-PD-1 resistance in human biliary cancer induce T cell paralysis [bulkRNA-seq]","description":"Suppressive myeloid cells can contribute to immunotherapy resistance, but their role in response to checkpoint inhibition (CPI) in anti-PD-1 refractory cancers, such as biliary tract cancer (BTC), is largely unknown. We use multiplexed single-cell transcriptomic and epitope sequencing to profile greater than 200,000 peripheral blood mononuclear cells from advanced BTC patients (n=9) and matched healthy donors (n=8). Following anti-PD-1 treatment, CD14+ monocytes expressing high levels of immunosuppressive cytokines and chemotactic molecules (CD14CTX) increase in the circulation of patients with BTC tumors that are CPI-resistant. CD14CTX can directly suppress CD4+ T cells and induce SOCS3 expression in CD4+ T cells rendering them functionally unresponsive. The CD14CTX gene signature associates with worse survival in patients with BTC as well as in other anti-PD-1 refractory cancers. These results demonstrate that monocytes arising after anti-PD-1 treatment can induce T cell paralysis as a distinct mode of tumor-mediated immunosuppression leading to CPI resistance.  Overall design: We performed bulkRNAseq on peripheral blood samples for use in demultiplexing single cell RNAseq data used in our publication. RNA was extracted from minimum 2.5 x 105 cells per PBMC sample and each sample was sequenced at a depth of at least 2 x 107 reads per cell on the Illumina Novaseq S4.","pubmed":"36130508","geo_series":"","n_samples":17,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN30466589","study_accession":"PRJNA872401","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Healthy donor-8, bulkseq","description":"Healthy donor-8, bulkseq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6481622","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-08-28","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["disease","Healthy"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21227476","experiment_accession":"SRX17237857","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":56011790,"base_count":16915560580,"first_public":"2022-08-28","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6481622: Healthy donor-8, bulkseq Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN30466590","study_accession":"PRJNA872401","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Healthy donor-7, bulkseq","description":"Healthy donor-7, bulkseq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6481621","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-08-28","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["disease","Healthy"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21227477","experiment_accession":"SRX17237856","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":61974286,"base_count":18716234372,"first_public":"2022-08-28","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6481621: Healthy donor-7, bulkseq Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN30466591","study_accession":"PRJNA872401","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Healthy donor-6, bulkseq","description":"Healthy donor-6, bulkseq","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6481620","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-08-28","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["cell_type","Peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["disease","Healthy"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR21227475","experiment_accession":"SRX17237858","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":66512624,"base_count":20086812448,"first_public":"2022-08-28","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequ